; One account holding two currencies — legal beancount, and the case gainstrack has to split
; into per-currency sub-accounts because it ties one account to one asset. This is the fixture
; that exercises the account-folding map.
option "operating_currency" "GBP"

2019-01-01 open Assets:Wallet
2019-01-01 open Assets:UkBank GBP
2019-01-01 open Income:Salary GBP
2019-01-01 open Expenses:Travel
2019-01-01 open Equity:Opening

2019-01-05 * "Employer" "January salary"
  Assets:UkBank    3000.00 GBP
  Income:Salary   -3000.00 GBP

; Cross-currency: a two-leg transfer at an explicit rate, which lifts to the two-amount `tfr`.
2019-02-01 * "Bureau" "Buy euros for the trip"
  Assets:Wallet      500.00 EUR @ 0.88 GBP
  Assets:UkBank     -440.00 GBP

2019-02-03 * "Cash withdrawal"
  Assets:Wallet      200.00 GBP
  Assets:UkBank     -200.00 GBP

2019-02-10 * "Hotel" "Paris"
  Expenses:Travel    180.00 EUR
  Assets:Wallet     -180.00 EUR

2019-02-11 * "Taxi" "Home from the airport"
  Expenses:Travel     35.00 GBP
  Assets:Wallet      -35.00 GBP

2019-03-01 balance Assets:Wallet 320.00 EUR
2019-03-01 balance Assets:Wallet 165.00 GBP
